        Yes. I checked the Jin Kazama page linked to Tekken Wiki
        Jin Kazama — the gist

        Jin Kazama is essentially the conflicted protagonist of Tekken: a fundamentally compassionate person caught between two very different inheritances.
            His mother is Jun Kazama, who raises him on Yakushima and teaches him self-control, self-defense, and a philosophy centered on harmony.
            His father is Kazuya Mishima, from the notoriously destructive Mishima bloodline. Jin also inherits the Devil Gene from Kazuya.
            At 15, Jin loses his mother when Ogre attacks. He goes to his grandfather Heihachi Mishima, who trains him for revenge.
            He eventually discovers that Heihachi himself intends to exploit him. After Jin defeats Ogre, Heihachi tries to kill him. The Devil Gene activates and saves Jin. TTekken Wiki 

        That betrayal fundamentally changes him.
        The interesting part: Jin isn't simply "good"

        Jin spends much of the series trying to escape what he believes he has inherited from the Mishimas—their violence, ambition, and Devil Gene.

        But in Tekken 6, his attempt to eliminate the Devil Gene becomes horribly distorted. He takes control of the Mishima Zaibatsu and deliberately plunges the world into war, believing that creating enough chaos will awaken Azazel, allowing him to destroy it and hopefully eradicate the Devil Gene. In doing so, he becomes responsible for enormous destruction despite believing his ultimate objective is justified. TTekken Wiki

        So there's a fascinating contradiction:

            Jin wants to destroy the evil inside himself, but sometimes becomes destructive in the process.

        And then Tekken 8 changes the direction

        By Tekken 8, Jin recognizes the consequences of what he did and wants to atone. His goal becomes stopping Kazuya and ending the Devil bloodline.

        More importantly, he begins learning that his Devil power doesn't necessarily have to control him. His journey becomes less about destroying himself or his bloodline and more about accepting himself and mastering what he has inherited. His reunion with Jun is particularly important to this development. TTekken Wiki
        In one sentence

        Jin Kazama is a good-hearted person fighting against the possibility that his inherited power, family history, and own hatred will turn him into the very thing he despises.

        And there's a neat symbolic detail: 仁 (Jin) means benevolence in Japanese, while Kazama uses characters associated with wind. TTekken Wiki

        The Jin Kazama page you provided

